## Phase 1 update (see .cursor/rules/*.mdc and .cursor/skills/*.md for detail)

This repo now also has structured rules under `.cursor/rules/` (project
overview, Rust conventions, Android conventions, safety/testing policy,
and VFS/SAF architecture) and reusable playbooks under `.cursor/skills/`.
If your Cursor version supports the newer `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` format,
read those directly — they're more current than this file for anything
Phase 1 related. Key changes since this file was originally written:

- **Test commands**: `cd rust && cargo test` now runs with NO flags and
  needs no Android SDK/NDK (default Cargo features are intentionally
  empty). Use `cargo check --features android --all-targets` to verify
  the JNI boundary type-checks.
- **`clippy::unwrap_used`/`clippy::expect_used` are enforced in CI as hard
  errors**, not just a style preference — see
  `.cursor/rules/30-safety-and-testing.mdc`.
- **VFS capability enforcement is now real**, not just documented: see
  `rust/src/vfs/service.rs` (`VfsService`, the thing that actually checks
  capabilities before calling a provider) and `rust/src/vfs/health.rs`
  (SAF permission staleness/revocation state machine). Route all file
  operations through `VfsService`, not directly through a `FsProvider`.
- `vfs_capabilities.rs` moved from the crate root to `rust/src/vfs/capabilities.rs`.
- Check `docs/PHASE1_STATUS.md` before assuming something is implemented.